.TH PSMatrixProductMV 3 2023-12-03 "PsyC 0.9.3" "PsyC Library Functions Manual"

.SH NAME
PSMatrixProductMV

.SH LIBRARY
PsyC (-lpsyc)

.SH SYNOPSIS

.B
#include <psyc/maths.h>

.I
int  
.br
\fBPSMatrixProductMV\fR(\fIPSMatrix a\fR, \fIPSFloat *b\fR, \fIint len\fR, \fIPSFloat ** result\fR, \fIPSMathOpts *opts\fR)
.SH DESCRIPTION
Performs matrix-vector multiplication between matrix \fIa\fR and vector \fIb\fR.
.br
Argument \fIlen\fR must be the length of the vector \fIb\fR.
.br
Results are stored into vector pointed by pointer \fIresult\fR. If pointer pointed by \fIresult\fR is \fINULL\fR, a new vector is automatically allocated by the function itself and its pointer will be stored into \fIresult\fR.
.br
Length of \fIb\fR vector must equal matrix \fIa\fR second dimension.
.br
Length of result vector must equal matrix \fIa\fR first dimension.
.br
By default, function uses BLAS to compute the result. Anyway, if BLAS support is missing in PsyC build, function will compute results by using \fIPSDotProduct\fR as fallback.
.br
You can set matrix transposition using \fItranspose\fR field in the \fIopt\fR argument. In that case, \fItranspose\fR will contain the (1-based) indices of the matrix arguments you want to be transposed:
.br

.RS 4
\[bu] opt->transpose = 1 (transpose matrix \fIa\fR)
.RE
.RE

By default, data in result vector will be overwritten. Anyway, if \fIPS_STORE_MODE_ADD\fR is set as \fIstore_mode\fR into \fIopts\fR, result will be added to data already present in the result vector.  

.SH RETURN VALUES
1 if operation succeeds, 0 if it fails.

.SH SEE ALSO
PSMatrixProduct(3), PSMatrixProductVM(3)
